James Kanze wrote:
> Doug Freyburger <dfrey...@yahoo.com> wrote:
>> James Kanze wrote:
>> > Doug Freyburger <dfrey...@yahoo.com> wrote:
>> >> A. Wyatt wrote:
>
>> >> >  a - an uncursed blindfold
>
>> >> I think this is better than a towel.
>
>> > Why?
>
>> The stats for blindfold and towel are identical - weight,
>> price, chance, so to me the only difference is a tiny bit of
>> simplicity -
>
>> A blind fold works by "a"pplying it ("P" works but it does not
>> appear in the list of options).  A towel works by "P"utting it
>> on and does something different when "a"pplied.  There's a
>> slightly greater typo risk with a towel accidentally taking
>> off an amulet or ring by mistake. That doesn't happen very
>> often but almost all of my characters die to typos.
>
> Good point; I've often accidentally removed a ring or an amulet
> thinking I was taking off a towel.
>
> I've generally gone with the towel because it had the additional
> effect, but I can't remember ever really needed that additional
> effect, so it's probably worth my changing tactics.

It's a tiny difference and it's a choice to go with the item that has
fewer uses.  That's not the usual way of NetHack players.  I
understand why better players than I will have the opposite
opinion.  But so many of my characters die to typos that I am
willing to make choices that reduce the impact of a single typo.
My preference of blindfold over towel is tiny and trivial but it is
neither random nor unconsidered - It's based on a known problem
with my playing skill.

But I don't remember ever dying because I ate a tin and monsters
killed me before I managed to wield my melee weapon again.  I
can hardly remember needing to pick up my melee weapon and
run while waiting for my hands to degrease.  And by the time I
encounter blinding attacks I tend to have telepathy.

But thinking I was taking off a towel and ending up taking off an
amulet of reflection, I've done that before I started preferring
blind folds.  I've done that since in games that gave me a towel but
not a blind fold.

Being able to wipe out messages in the dust is an interesting
opinion.  I've never tried it.  Messages in the dust before arriving
on a level are rare enough that I've never tried it.


